  m_Name: 1966bilingual
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Bilingual Policy (1966)
  info: Upon independence, Singapore implemented the bilingual education policy,
    requiring students to learn English as a first language and their mother tongue
    as a second language. This policy aimed to promote cultural roots while ensuring
    global competitiveness. It remains a cornerstone of the education system today.
